// Bessel functions of integer order: J0, J1, Y0, Y1, I0, I1, K0, K1 and
// the scaled forms, then any order n by recurrence.
//
// The layout is Cephes' (Moshier): below 8 (1 for K) a series in x^2
// with the logarithmic part split off (I: e^-x I in x), above it the Hankel form
// sqrt(2 / (pi x)) (P cos chi - Q sin chi) with P and Q smooth in
// 64 / x^2 (I and K: their decaying factor removed). The coefficients
// are Chebyshev expansions refitted to 60-digit mpmath values and cut
// below 1e-19. J0 and J1 carry their first two zeros as factors
// (x - z) (x + z), with z split into two doubles, so they keep full
// relative accuracy at those zeros.

use pkg::bessel::cheb;
use pkg::bessel::real::series;

const SQRT_PI: f64 = 1.7724538509055160;
const FRAC_2_PI: f64 = 0.6366197723675814;
